635 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1295 0 R
/E (Our research develops Turkey's first agent-based ETS simulation framework to provide evidence-based guidance for climate policy design before the 2026 EU CBAM deadline. We systematically reviewed 133 studies, identified a critical research gap, and designed a modeling framework with three agent types and five policy scenarios. Our findings demonstrate that Turkey can transform the CBAM threat into an economic opportunity while achieving significant emission reductions aligned with NDC targets. In the first term, we completed the conceptual design, data integration and initial model setup; we are currently in the development and testing phase, with simulation runs and comprehensive analysis planned for completion in the second term to finalize policy recommendations guiding Turkey's three phase ETS establishment.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [3]
>>
